UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: Death represents the absolute archetype of ''Systemic Deprecation and Radical Transmutation''—the inescapable, high-priority phase where the sovereign consciousness executes a total purge of obsolete, low-integrity structures, clear-cutting legacy code to make room for a completely fresh evolutionary architecture. Moving beyond the voluntary suspension of The Hanged Man, Death signifies the stage of ''The Final Garbage Collector,'' where you purposefully dismantle attachments, dead relationships, and outdated identities that no longer serve your core processor. Visually depicted as a skeletal knight in black armor riding a powerful white horse, trampling a fallen king while a child and a young woman kneel in supplication before a bishop, all under a dark sky where the sun rises between two distant towers, this archetype embodies the concept of ''Structural Impermanence''—the realization that true spiritual and mental mastery requires the courage to let things end cleanly, without dragging the dead weight of the past into the emergent cycle. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of ''Hard Deletion and Defragmentation,'' where you drop corrupted database tables, terminate zombie processes, and completely clear your memory cache to allow a brand-new operating phase to initialize. When Death appears, your system is registering a ''Terminal-Purge'' status; you are being invited to stop resisting the natural decay of your old world, embrace the absolute liberation of a clean slate, and allow the fire of transformation to refine your domain.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When Death appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of ''Systemic Stagnation, Inability to Let Go, or Chronic Resistance to Renewal''—a dangerous state where you are frantically attempting to run obsolete, broken code, keeping a dead structure on life support out of sheer fear of the unknown. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates ''clinging to a toxic routine, nursing dead illusions, or resisting a necessary transition'' with ''being loyal and stable,'' even as your actual, internal operating system is experiencing a critical, low-latency drag from severe energetic decay. You are essentially ''saturating your memory buffers with dead processes,'' running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to ''avoid the discomfort of grief and structural collapse'' over the sober, unglamorous requirement to let the old system die and bury its dead. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the ''unmoved, timeless protector of the past,'' while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of decay, chronic anxiety, or unmitigated dread, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of ''living in an artificial, claustrophobic loop of your own making,'' and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your current security is a decaying illusion. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a ''feedback loop of resistance and slow spiritual asphyxiation''; you are obsessively avoiding the cemetery of your past, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final resurrection of your spirit is your own, deep-seated fear that if you were to open your hands and let the old structures crumble completely, you would be forced to confront the terrifying reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these change-resistant, stagnation-inducing scripts, perform a brutal audit of your attachments, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize structural clean-slating over the convenience of a familiar, rotting cage. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance stagnation, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority.'
WHERE id = 70;
